# Generated from the OSRS Wiki page "Transcript:Sheep Shearer" by tools/quests/transcript_to_dialogue.py
0	section	Starting off
1	line	Fred the Farmer	What are you doing on my land? You're not the one who keeps leaving all my gates open and letting out all my sheep, are you?
1	select	Select an option
1	option	I'm looking for a quest.
2	line	Player	I'm looking for a quest.
2	cond	On quest speedrunning worlds:
3	line	Fred the Farmer	You're after a quest, you say? Well I don't have any here.
3	box	This quest is not available on Speedrunning Worlds.
2	line	Fred the Farmer	You're after a quest, you say? Actually, I could do with a bit of help.
2	line	Fred the Farmer	My sheep are getting mighty woolly. I'd be much obliged if you could shear them. And while you're at it, spin the wool for me too.
2	line	Fred the Farmer	Yes, that's it. Bring me 20 balls of wool. And I'm sure I could sort out some sort of payment. Of course, there's the small matter of The Thing.
2	action	If the player already has 20 balls of wool in their inventory:
3	line	Player	In fact Fred, funnily enough, I actually have 20 balls of wool already on me.
3	line	Fred the Farmer	Have you been shearing my sheep without permission!?
3	line	Player	No! Well, maybe... They just looked a little wooly! Surely you like a shave once in a while, too?
3	line	Fred the Farmer	It's rude to shave another person without permission - don't be coming at me with them shears!
3	line	Player	I'm sorry, I'll ask permission next time.
3	line	Fred the Farmer	I guess no real 'arm was done. Hand the balls over and we can put this whole thing behind us.
3	action	end
2	line	Player	What do you mean, The Thing?
2	line	Fred the Farmer	Well now, no one has ever seen The Thing. That's why we call it The Thing, 'cos we don't know what it is.
2	line	Fred the Farmer	Some say it's a black hearted shapeshifter, hungering for the souls of hard working decent folk like me. Others say it's just a sheep.
2	line	Fred the Farmer	Well I don't have all day to stand around and gossip. Are you going to shear my sheep or what!
2	select	Start the Sheep Shearer quest?
2	option	Yes.
3	line	Player	Yes, okay. I can do that.
3	line	Fred the Farmer	Good! Now one more thing, do you actually know how to shear a sheep?
3	line	Player	Err. No, I don't know actually.
3	cond	If the player doesn't have shears:
3	line	Fred the Farmer	Well, first things first, you need a pair of shears. I've got some here you can use.
3	box	Fred gives you a set of sharp shears.
4	line	Fred the Farmer	You just need to go and use them on the sheep out in my field.
4	line	Player	Sounds easy!
4	line	Fred the Farmer	That's what they all say!
4	line	Fred the Farmer	Some of the sheep don't like it too much... Persistence is the key.
4	line	Fred the Farmer	Once you've collected some wool you can spin it into balls.
4	action	continues
3	cond	If the player has shears already:
4	line	Fred the Farmer	Well, you're half way there already! You have a set of shears in your inventory. Just use those on a Sheep to shear it.
4	line	Player	That's all I have to do?
4	line	Fred the Farmer	Well once you've collected some wool you'll need to spin it into balls.
4	action	continues
3	line	Fred the Farmer	Do you know how to spin wool?
3	line	Player	I don't know how to spin wool, sorry.
3	line	Fred the Farmer	Don't worry, it's quite simple!
3	line	Fred the Farmer	The nearest Spinning Wheel can be found on the first floor of Lumbridge Castle.
3	line	Fred the Farmer	To get to Lumbridge Castle just follow the road east.
3	box	This icon denotes a Spinning Wheel on the world map.
3	line	Player	Thank you!
3	action	end
2	option	No.
3	line	Player	No, I'll give it a miss.
3	line	Fred the Farmer	Suit yourself.
3	action	end
